- op: discuss  # ac9b
  at: '2026-04-30T18:57:19Z'  # ac9b
  by: agent  # ac9b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ac9b
  clock: 4  # ac9b
  nonce: ac9b  # ac9b
  message: "Agree, marking wont_do. The principled point is sharper than just 'release timing is bad' — it's that audit triggers should couple to *slack*, not to *deadlines*, and per-release is anti-correlated with slack precisely because release prep is when we want the mechanics to operate fast. The 72-commit cadence (PR #3460) is calendar-orthogonal, so it's more likely to fire on a normal day when there's bandwidth to handle whatever it surfaces. Two follow-on implications: (1) WI-juvaf-pubib-kiguh-kubat-jagiv-sigad-jikav-gumag's deliverable 1 (per-release bake-in for the generative question) inherits the same risk and likely needs rescoping — surfaced for review there; (2) the audit playbook's anti-pattern list already names 'mid-feature' as a slack-anti-correlation; the same shape applies to release prep and is worth generalizing into a 'audit triggers couple to slack' principle."  # ac9b
